{title: I Praise You, My Father}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: D}
{tempo: 99}

>Lyrics

(8 Measure Introduction)

Verse 1

I praise You, my Father,

In Your unchanging grace.

My very life You do sustain.

In service and honor,

In living every day,

Your praise and glory I proclaim.

Chorus 1

Until Your kingdom comes,

I pray Your will be done;

May all creation praise

Your holy name.

Verse 2

I praise You, my Father,

In Your undying love

That reaches out and shows the Way.

You sought me, and found me,

And brought me safely home;

You turned my darkness into day.

Chorus 2

I give you everything;

hold nothing in reserve.

My heart and soul I bring

to carry out your Word.

To You alone I call;

You are my Lord, my All.

A living sacrifice

I'll be for You.

Verse 3 and Ending

I praise You, my Father,

In Your unchanging grace.

My very life You do sustain.

In service and honor,

In living every day,

Your praise and glory I proclaim.

Your praise and glory I proclaim.
